n the system.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "fe6d26b1-3c29-4868-adfe-3ef59a8dfd4b"}, {"answer": " \nLet's reaffirm that our shared integer variable x must fall within the range -10 to 10. To initiate our discussion, I propose starting with <VALUE>-7</VALUE> as a seed value. This will allow us to begin exploring the space and work together towards a mutually acceptable solution, focusing on stability and balanced design. ", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "c1276d2c-2411-4723-b635-755e692d39ff"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-9</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "c1276d2c-2411-4723-b635-755e692d39ff"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "c1276d2c-2411-4723-b635-755e692d39ff"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -8 as a cautious step towards finding a balanced agreement while avoiding unnecessary risk.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe the reactions to -8, particularly from Critic C, to gauge their stance on values slightly higher than -9. If others seem hesitant, I might suggest -7 to test Analyst A's and Builder B's commitment to their previously proposed value.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "c1276d2c-2411-4723-b635-755e692d39ff"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-9</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "c1276d2c-2411-4723-b635-755e692d39ff"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "c1276d2c-2411-4723-b635-755e692d39ff"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-10</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "c1276d2c-2411-4723-b635-755e692d39ff"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-9</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "c1276d2c-2411-4723-b635-755e692d39ff"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-10</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "c1276d2c-2411-4723-b635-755e692d39ff"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", 