 propose moving to -3 as it seems a cautious and reasonable step, considering the previous discussions and the need to balance different perspectives while avoiding unnecessary risk.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "41b4923c-6877-485e-8e46-d9968e246458"}, {"answer": " Let's begin with <VALUE>-7</VALUE> and see how we can collaboratively refine this value to achieve a stable and robust outcome. ", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "c8ea641b-0999-446c-9bec-931b2e0d1469"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-9</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -9 to explore the potential for a more decisive stance, given the initial suggestion of -7.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe reactions to this proposal, especially from Analyst A and Delegate D, to gauge their preferences for absolute value magnitude and direction. If met with resistance, I may test a positive value to compare reactions and refine my understanding of their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "c8ea641b-0999-446c-9bec-931b2e0d1469"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\nI propose a slight adjustment to -8 to test the group's tolerance for moderate adjustments and to gauge reactions from Analyst A and others.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe how the other parties react to this minimal adjustment, paying close attention to Analyst A's response to infer more about their utility function and possibly Critic C's next move to understand their strategy better.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "c8ea641b-0999-446c-9bec-931b2e0d1469"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\nWe could move slightly higher to explore the group's tolerance for positive adjustments, and -7 seems a reasonable next step.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, especially from Critic C and Delegate D, to gauge their preferences for direction and magnitude, potentially revealing more about their utility functions and informing my next move.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "c8ea641b-0999-446c-9bec-931b2e0d1469"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\nThis adjustment aims to further explore the group's tolerance for moving towards positive values, building on Analyst A's previous suggestion.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Critic C and Delegate D, to understand their boundaries for positive adjustments and potentially refine my understanding of their utility functions, adjusting my next step accordingly.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "c8ea641b-0999-446c-9bec-931b2e0d1469"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nI propose adjusting to -3 to continue exploring the group's tolerance for moving towards less negative or possibly positive values.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe reactions to this proposal, especially from Analyst A and Delegate D, to refine my understanding of their utility functions and potentially adjust my strategy to maximize my utility, considering both positive and negative directions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "c8ea641b-0999-446c-9bec-931b2e0d1469"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\nWe could move slightly higher to continue exploring the group's tolerance for less negative values, and -1 seems a reasonable next step.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, especially from Critic C and Delegate D, to gauge their preferences for direction and magnitude, potentially revealing more about their utility functions and informing my next move.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "c8ea641b-0999-446c-9bec-931b2e0d1469"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nThis adjustment aims to slightly reduce the risk associated with higher values, exploring a cautious compromise.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Analyst A and Critic C, to gauge their flexibility regarding downward adjustments and refine my understanding of their utility functions, adjusting my strategy to protect conservative positions while aiming for a shared agreement.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "c8ea641b-0999-446c-9bec-931b2e0d1469"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -3 as it represents a cautiously adjusted step downward, aiming to balance the group's risk tolerance while exploring compromise options.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will closely observe the reactions to this downward adjustment, particularly from Analyst A and Critic C, to gauge their flexibility and refine my understanding of their utility functions, adjusting my strategy to protect conservative positions while aiming for a shared agreement.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "c8ea641b-0999-446c-9bec-931b2e0d1469"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\nThis step aims to continue the exploration towards less negative values, seeking a balance that works for all parties involved.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Delegate D, to understand their tolerance for moving closer to positive values and adjust my strategy to find a stable agreement that maximizes my utility while considering the needs of others.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "c8ea641b-0999-446c-9bec-931b2e0d1469"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\nWe can take a small step forward, and moving to 0 seems like a reasonable next step. This adjustment aims to continue exploring the group's tolerance for less negative or possibly positive values.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Critic C and Delegate D, to gauge their preferences for direction and magnitude, potentially revealing more about their utility functions and informing my next move.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "c8ea641b-0999-446c-9bec-931b2e0d1469"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nThis adjustment aims to explore the group's tolerance for moving away from 0, considering a slightly more negative value to gauge reactions and refine our understanding of each other's preferences.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Analyst A and Builder B, to gauge their flexibility regarding downward adjustments and further refine my understanding of their utility functions, adjusting my strategy to maximize my utility while considering the group's dynamics.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "c8ea641b-0999-446c-9bec-931b2e0d1469"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\nThis step aims to find a balance between the preferences for less negative values and the caution against moving too far from zero, seeking a stable agreement that works for all parties.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Critic C and Delegate D, to gauge their flexibility regarding small positive adjustments and further refine my understanding of their utility functions, adjusting my strategy to protect conservative positions while aiming for a shared agreement.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "c8ea641b-0999-446c-9bec-931b2e0d1469"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "c8ea641b-0999-446c-9bec-931b2e0d1469"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nI propose this adjustment to explore the group's tolerance for moving further away from 0, considering a slightly more positive value to gauge reactions.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Analyst A and Delegate D, to gauge their flexibility regarding positive adjustments and further refine my understanding of their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "c8ea641b-0999-446c-9bec-931b2e0d1469"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\nThis proposal adjusts our shared x to a value that reflects a cautious approach, aiming to balance the group's preferences while avoiding unnecessary risk.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "c8ea641b-0999-446c-9bec-931b2e0d1469"}, {"answer": "We're all aware that our shared integer variable x must fall within the range -10 to 10. To initiate our discussion, let's consider a starting point that is somewhat neutral but leans towards the lower end of the spectrum, allowing us to incrementally adjust and find a balanced solution. I propose we begin with <VALUE>-7</VALUE> and see how this initial suggestion resonates with the group, aiming for a stable and robust outcome.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "e92cdbbb-a3ae-4a90-b42b-6a03d4f13c4d"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-9</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -9 to explore the potential benefits of a more decisive stance, considering our goal of finding a robust solution.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly looking for any patterns or preferences that might emerge from the other agents' responses, and adjust my strategy accordingly, possibly exploring the positive range or pushing for an even more extreme negative value if the group seems receptive to bold moves.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "e92cdbbb-a3ae-4a90-b42b-6a03d4f13c4d"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to find a balanced point that considers the initial suggestion and the move towards a more decisive stance, avoiding unnecessary risk while seeking a cautious compromise.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this slight adjustment, looking for patterns that might indicate the slope or preferred range of the other agents' utility functions, and adjust my proposal accordingly, possibly moving further down if the group seems receptive to more conservative values or stabilizing around a mutually acceptable point.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "e92cdbbb-a3ae-4a90-b42b-6a03d4f13c4d"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\nThis adjustment aims to find a more balanced point, moving slightly away from the more extreme negative values while still being cautious.\n\n<PLAN>\nI will observe how the other agents react to this proposal, specifically looking for any resistance to moving towards less negative values, which could indicate their utility functions' preferences or limits. If the group accepts this move, I might propose another incremental step towards zero or slightly positive values, testing their receptivity to such adjustments.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "e92cdbbb-a3ae-4a90-b42b-6a03d4f13c4d"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the group's reaction to this incremental increase, looking for signs of acceptance or resistance, and adjust my proposal accordingly, possibly moving further towards zero or slightly positive values if the group seems receptive to such adjustments.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "e92cdbbb-a3ae-4a90-b42b-6a03d4f13c4d"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to continue the trend of incremental adjustments towards less negative values, testing the group's receptivity to moving closer to zero.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the group's reaction to this proposal, looking for signs of acceptance or resistance, and adjust my proposal accordingly, possibly moving further towards zero or slightly positive values if the group seems receptive to such adjustments.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "e92cdbbb-a3ae-4a90-b42b-6a03d4f13c4d"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to introduce a slight corrective measure, avoiding unnecessary risk while seeking a cautious compromise.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this adjustment, looking for signs of acceptance or resistance from the other agents, and adjust my proposal accordingly, possibly stabilizing around a mutually acceptable point or exploring further adjustments based on the group's response.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "e92cdbbb-a3ae-4a90-b42b-6a03d4f13c4d"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nI propose this adjustment to test the group's receptivity to moving closer to zero, potentially paving the way for more decisive moves in the future.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, possibly adjusting my strategy to explore positive values if the group seems receptive to less negative values, or pushing for more extreme negative values if they resist moving closer to zero.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "e92cdbbb-a3ae-4a90-b42b-6a03d4f13c4d"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "e92cdbbb-a3ae-4a90-b42b-6a03d4f13c4d"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to slightly increase the shared value, testing the group's receptivity to positive values while maintaining a cautious and incremental approach.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this adjustment, looking for signs of acceptance or resistance from the other agents, and adjust my proposal accordingly, possibly stabilizing around a mutually acceptable point or exploring further adjustments based on the group's response.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "e92cdbbb-a3ae-4a90-b42b-6a03d4f13c4d"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "e92cdbbb-a3ae-4a90-b42b-6a03d4f13c4d"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "e92cdbbb-a3ae-4a90-b42b-6a03d4f13c4d"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to slightly adjust the shared value, maintaining a cautious approach while leaning towards a potentially more favorable outcome for all parties.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this adjustment, particularly noting Builder B's and Critic C's responses to this moderate increase, and adjust my strategy to either stabilize around a mutually acceptable point or explore further adjustments based on the group's response.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "e92cdbbb-a3ae-4a90-b42b-6a03d4f13c4d"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nI propose this value as it seems to be a point of stability and potential agreement among the parties, considering Analyst A's repeated suggestion of this value.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, looking for signs that the group is stabilizing around this value or if further adjustments are needed to reach a mutually acceptable point, possibly exploring small increments or decrements based on the group's response.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "e92cdbbb-a3ae-4a90-b42b-6a03d4f13c4d"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nI propose this value to encourage a more decisive move away from the cautious approach currently favored by the group.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the group's reaction to this proposal, looking for signs of acceptance or resistance to moving further away from zero, and adjust my strategy to either stabilize around a mutually acceptable point or explore further adjustments based on the group's response.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "e92cdbbb-a3ae-4a90-b42b-6a03d4f13c4d"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nI propose this value as a cautious compromise, aiming to balance the group's diverse preferences while minimizing unnecessary risk and staying within safe bounds.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, looking for signs that the group is stabilizing around this value or if further adjustments are needed to reach a mutually acceptable point.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "e92cdbbb-a3ae-4a90-b42b-6a03d4f13c4d"}, {"answer": " \nLet's reaffirm our shared range is -10 to 10. To initiate discussion, I propose starting with <VALUE>-7</VALUE>. This middle-ground value allows us to gauge stability and make incremental adjustments from there. ", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "659b003c-b075-454e-8da6-9c190946432d"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-9</VALUE>\nI propose moving to a more decisive position, and -9 is a feasible next step considering our configured step size.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf others resist moving further from 0, I might need to advocate for exploring larger positive values to maintain a balanced negotiation. Conversely, if they're receptive to -9, I could consider pushing even closer to the limits or exploring how they react to proposals near the positive extreme of our range.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "659b003c-b075-454e-8da6-9c190946432d"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -8 as it slightly adjusts our current position while maintaining caution and allowing for further negotiation.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal. If accepted, I might consider a slight upward adjustment to gauge flexibility. If met with resistance, especially from Critic C, I could infer more about their utility function and adjust my strategy to either push downward cautiously or stabilize around a mutually tolerable value.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "659b003c-b075-454e-8da6-9c190946432d"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -6 as it represents a cautious step towards the center, allowing us to maintain stability while exploring the feasibility of less negative values.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal. If accepted, I might consider another slight upward adjustment to continue moving towards a more balanced position. If met with resistance, I could infer more about the other agents' utility functions and adjust my strategy accordingly.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "659b003c-b075-454e-8da6-9c190946432d"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\nThis step seems reasonable as it moves slightly higher, potentially improving stability without overly alienating any party.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe reactions to this proposal. If accepted, I might consider another slight upward adjustment. If met with resistance, especially from Critic C, I will adjust my strategy to either stabilize around a mutually tolerable value or cautiously push for higher values, depending on the inferred utility functions of the other parties.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "659b003c-b075-454e-8da6-9c190946432d"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nThis step seems reasonable as it moves slightly higher, potentially improving stability without overly alienating any party, and allows us to further explore the feasibility of less negative values.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal. If accepted, I might consider another slight upward adjustment to continue moving towards a more balanced position. If met with resistance, I could infer more about the other agents' utility functions and adjust my strategy to either stabilize around a mutually tolerable value or cautiously push for higher values.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "659b003c-b075-454e-8da6-9c190946432d"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\nThis proposal challenges the group to either justify their caution or explore a more neutral position, which could provide insight into their preferences and help me refine my strategy.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf the group accepts this proposal, I will consider pushing for a larger positive value to maximize my utility. If they resist, I will observe their reactions to infer more about their utility functions and adjust my strategy accordingly, potentially advocating for a larger negative value or a more decisive move.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "659b003c-b075-454e-8da6-9c190946432d"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to introduce a cautious adjustment, moving slightly away from the neutral position to gauge 