 {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nThis proposal seems like a reasonable next step, considering the back-and-forth between -5 and -3, and it slightly increases the value of x, which could be beneficial for most parties involved.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe how the other agents react to this proposal, particularly looking for any signs that they might be willing to accept further increases in x or if they push back, indicating potential limits to their utility functions. Based on their responses, I can adjust my subsequent proposal to either continue guiding the negotiation towards higher x values or to stabilize around a mutually acceptable point.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "b1f0673f-6c00-4d7e-8676-d73598103109"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\nThis adjustment aims to continue the gradual increase in x, testing the waters for a potential move towards positive values while maintaining stability and robustness in our shared solution.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, especially looking for any signs of acceptance or resistance to moving closer to or into the positive range. Based on the responses, I will either continue to guide the negotiation towards higher x values or adjust my strategy to stabilize around a mutually acceptable point, refining my understanding of the other agents' utility functions to maximize my own utility.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "b1f0673f-6c00-4d7e-8676-d73598103109"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nThis proposal adjusts our shared variable to a value that was previously discussed and seemed acceptable to some parties, allowing us to reassess preferences and potentially move towards a more decisive stance.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe reactions to this proposal, looking for signs that agents are receptive to revisiting previously considered values or if they push for further increases in x, guiding my subsequent proposal to maximize my utility while considering the apparent preferences of the group.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "b1f0673f-6c00-4d7e-8676-d73598103109"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nI propose this adjustment as it represents a cautious step towards a potentially more mutually beneficial value, while avoiding unnecessary risk.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe how the other agents react to this proposal, looking for signs that they are receptive to small adjustments in x, and adjust my subsequent proposal accordingly to maximize my utility while maintaining a cautious approach.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "b1f0673f-6c00-4d7e-8676-d73598103109"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "b1f0673f-6c00-4d7e-8676-d73598103109"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\nThis proposal continues the gradual trend towards more positive values, aiming for a balanced and stable solution that works for all parties. It's a cautious step forward, testing the group's willingness to enter the positive range.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe reactions to this proposal, looking for signs of acceptance or resistance to entering the positive range, and adjust my strategy to either continue guiding the negotiation towards higher x values or stabilize around a mutually acceptable point, refining my understanding of the other agents' utility functions.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "b1f0673f-6c00-4d7e-8676-d73598103109"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nThis proposal continues the trend towards more positive values, aiming for a more decisive stance while considering the group's willingness to enter the positive range.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe reactions to this proposal, looking for signs of acceptance or resistance to increasing x further, and adjust my strategy accordingly to maximize my utility while considering the apparent preferences of the group.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_nu